source: crates/holst-cli/src/table.rs
expression: help_of(line)
---
Download the original of an image or file object.
The file goes to ~/Downloads under its own name unless a file or --dir says otherwise; it only reads the board.

USAGE
  holst object get <board> [<file>] [flags]

ARGUMENTS
  board   The board: id, link or part of its name
  file    A new file, never overwritten, - for stdout; the object's own name in ~/Downloads by default

FLAGS
      --object object   An object: id, link, @N or the first 8 characters of its id
  -w, --workspace ws    Where names are looked up and new things go: a workspace id or part of its name; all of yours by default
      --dir dir         The local folder it goes into under its own name; ~/Downloads by default
      --refresh         Ignore the cached copy and download the board again

INHERITED FLAGS
  --output, --verbose, --base-url, --home, --no-cache, --help   as in `holst -h`

EXAMPLES
  $ holst o get "Roadmap" --object a1b2c3d4
  $ holst o get "Roadmap" --object a1b2c3d4 mock.png

LEARN MORE
  How a board is given: `holst b -h`.
  Exit codes: `holst help exit-codes`.
